      "title": "Troubleshooting Certificate Expiration and Credential Propagation Issues in SSO",
      "content_summary": "Addresses common SSO integration errors including expired certificates, missing audit logs, and unexpected logouts related to credential rotation delays.",
      "content_body": "When users encounter certificate expired warnings or unexpected logouts, first verify the validity period of the active signing certificate within the SSO Integration Module. Missing entries in audit logs are often a known product limitation when high-volume traffic occurs simultaneously with certificate updates. If elevated privileges or access denied errors persist after renewing certificates, check for propagation delays in credential rotation across connected identity providers. Standard resolution involves scheduling certificate renewals during low-traffic windows and allowing 5-10 minutes for credential changes to sync. In cases where unexpected behavior matches documented limitations, confirm that no fix is required as the system is operating as designed."
